<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/855314-the-sundered-world?p=858477#post858477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the Mastigoi known as? Thought-Wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forest-Wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:37:29-07:00","id":858496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/855314-the-sundered-world?p=858477#post858477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the Mastigoi known as? Thought-Wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forest-Wise, which is how they perceive the dark labyrinth (not that they have the concept of labyrinths) of the mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:41:47-07:00","id":858499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/855314-the-sundered-world?p=858477#post858477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the Mastigoi known as? Thought-Wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Acanthus are Sky-Wise, Mastigos are Forest-Wise, Moros are Sea-Wise (I maintain that Water-Wise is a typo), Obrimos are Storm-Wise, and Thyrsus are Blood-Wise. All Paths have a claim to sumbolic fire, which is the most common metaphor for Awakening at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T03:21:41-07:00","id":858860,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the idea of meeting other cultures and their archetypes in the Temenos, and what contemporary cultures might be contacted, so here's a first one...<br /> <br /> The Halaf (south-eastern Anatolia, northern Syria &amp; Iraq) are a fellow copper-wielding civilization, so in the Astral their representation tends to be found not far from the Vinca. While they haven't unlocked the mysteries of High Speech like the Vinca, their Wise do know secrets of personal property as sympathetic links via stamp-seals. They worship a powerful mother/fertility goddess, a Pangean embodiment of sex and childbirth who spends most of her existence in the Astral to mingle with her worshippers and evade Wolf. This culture has more contact with the Gudthabak (werebulls) than the Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-04-2016, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:28:56-07:00","id":858950,"title":"","content":"The Hemudu (coastal China, south of where the Yellow River civilizations will prosper, closer ethnically related to Austranesian peoples than the modern Chinese) worship Glorious Sun first and foremost, and Bird second. They share kinship with the Surthu Athilal (the werefalcons). In the process of domesticating rice, they are also a innovative fishing society known for their stilt huts, which in the Astral are towering avian perches over idealized fishing waters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:29:38-07:00","id":858951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/855314-the-sundered-world?p=858860#post858860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the idea of meeting other cultures and their archetypes in the Temenos, and what contemporary cultures might be contacted, so here's a first one...<br /> <br /> The Halaf (south-eastern Anatolia, northern Syria &amp; Iraq) are a fellow copper-wielding civilization, so in the Astral their representation tends to be found not far from the Vinca. While they haven't unlocked the mysteries of High Speech like the Vinca, their Wise do know secrets of personal property as sympathetic links via stamp-seals. They worship a powerful mother/fertility goddess, a Pangean embodiment of sex and childbirth who spends most of her existence in the Astral to mingle with her worshippers and evade Wolf. This culture has more contact with the Gudthabak (werebulls) than the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea! Looking at the Vinca's neighbors to the north and west, the LBK culture, I wonder how the setting would inform the differences with the Vinca? The LBK were a more sedentary people with walled villages and apparently the first signs of organized warfare. There is even debate over whether or net they practiced cannibalism, some archaeologists think they cannibalized their enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:53:21-07:00","id":858964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/855314-the-sundered-world?p=858951#post858951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great idea! Looking at the Vinca's neighbors to the north and west, the LBK culture, I wonder how the setting would inform the differences with the Vinca? The LBK were a more sedentary people with walled villages and apparently the first signs of organized warfare. There is even debate over whether or net they practiced cannibalism, some archaeologists think they cannibalized their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely lean into Herxheim-evidence to give them a distinct setting niche (cannibalism, secondary burial, skull cult...) OH! What if instead of &quot;the Wise&quot; - the Returned (Sin-Eaters) have the place of honor in their society?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T07:03:47-07:00","id":858973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/855314-the-sundered-world?p=858964#post858964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd definitely lean into Herxheim-evidence to give them a distinct setting niche (cannibalism, secondary burial, skull cult...) OH! What if instead of &quot;the Wise&quot; - the Returned (Sin-Eaters) have the place of honor in their society?</div> </div> </div> </div>And incorporate my third favorite splat in CofD? Yes, please. Would the Thresholds need any alteration? I would think not as death is sort of an eternal constant. With the warfare the Torn could be more heavily represented in this culture than in the Vinca.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T07:18:34-07:00","id":858979,"title":"","content":"I want to report that I had a session of Neolithic Mage last night and it was pretty fun, even more than what I expected. Dunno how long we can continue it, perhaps at least just another session for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T07:27:21-07:00","id":858984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/855314-the-sundered-world?p=858973#post858973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And incorporate my third favorite splat in CofD? Yes, please. Would the Thresholds need any alteration? I would think not as death is sort of an eternal constant. With the warfare the Torn could be more heavily represented in this culture than in the Vinca.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Bound in general are more common. They're proportionally rarer in the Neolithic era than modern day because of the nature of the Underworld, but the LBK have specific rites to encourage the return even a fair amount of time after death... I'll fiddle with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:20:53-07:00","id":859689,"title":"","content":"Popped another Pangaean up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859687#post859687\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859687#post859687\"> Pangaea Unleashed - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859687#post859687\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859687#post859687 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So Dark Eras is out to backers and, with it, the Neolithic era covering Mage and Werewolf. Thoughts? Criticisms? Any interest in me writing up some unofficial sample Pangaeans? Sadly I didn't have wordcount to do more than provide the basic Pangaean rules in the chapter. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200bNext on my list are some sample spirits.<br /> <br /> Usual disclaimer: This is all unofficial. I'd have liked to have had the space for sample Pangaeans and spirits in the Sundered World but didn't have the word count; equally, that means that these are *not* an official addition to TSW and in no way meant to close off peoples' own ideas and notions for creating Pangaeans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:56:23-07:00","id":859900,"title":"","content":"So I have only barely skimmed the Hellenic Mage Era at this point and I would need a much deeper reading before I start a new topic, but since my question is also related to this Era I'll ask it here: the metaphysics of the world are described vastly differently in the Neolithic while on a quick skim the supernatural world in Alexander's time is mostly the same as modern day. <br /> <br /> Am I misreading the Hellenic section and it's caught somewhere in the middle of a transition, or do you think it's a factor of more than just time? I'm not just talking about the Paths but also stuff like the Underworld. Any thoughts would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:03:56-07:00","id":859907,"title":"","content":"Two things...<br /> <br /> 1) the Sundering is a pretty massive change that isn't at all gradual<br /> <br /> 2) To the Strongest is twice as far from Sundered World as it is from present day chronologically. Plenty of time for the Ocean Beyond Life to recede into the Rivers of the Dead.<br /> <br /> The cool transition in the Hellenistic period is in Mage society (the birth of the Diamond Orders) not metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T01:34:49-07:00","id":860174,"title":"","content":"Ok, the example contemporaries of the Vinca one might run into in the Astral I have so far...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Halaf (south-eastern Anatolia, northern Syria &amp; Iraq) are a fellow copper-wielding civilization, so in the Astral their representation tends to be found not far from the Vinca. While they haven't unlocked the mysteries of High Speech like the Vinca, their Wise do know secrets of personal property as sympathetic links via stamp-seals. They worship a powerful mother/fertility goddess, a Pangean embodiment of sex and childbirth who spends most of her existence in the Astral to mingle with her worshippers and evade Wolf. This culture has more contact with the Gudthabak (werebulls) than the Uratha.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Hemudu (coastal China, south of where the Yellow River civilizations will prosper, closer ethnically related to Austranesian peoples than the modern Chinese) worship Glorious Sun first and foremost, and Bird second. They share kinship with the Surthu Athilal (the werefalcons). In the process of domesticating rice, they are also a innovative fishing society known for their stilt huts, which in the Astral are towering avian perches over idealized fishing waters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Vinca's neighbors to the north are today known as the LBK (linear pottery) culture. Less advanced than the copper and High Speech wielding Vinca, they're comparatively more sedentary, building defensive earthworks around their villages as they live among often raiding hunting-gatherers from the north that the Vinca do not. Once they worshipped the same Mother Goddess as the Halafa, but a new religion of macabre ancestor worship and promised resurrection is being spread among their villages by men and women returned from the Ocean Beyond Life. This new religion involves rites of secondary-burial (exhuming the dead), cannibalism, and skull-worship. The Returned display a mastery of the dead terrifying to even the Water-Wise, and unrestrained by dissonance or quiesence. Some of the Wise of LBK settlements (who never held the same place of honor as their Vinca counterparts) are fleeing elsewhere.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Around the Black Sea, coming south out of the Caucuses, a pastoralist nomad culture of cattle and goat herders (still a millennium or so away from domesticated horses). Not yet mastering agriculture, this society would be of little note, were it not that their primary deity, a great thunder-eyed, cloud-bearded Shepherd is such a boisterous presence in the Astral. No sign of any existence as a Pangean, he may entirely be an Astral archetype of human shepherding. He desires to claim the Halaf mother goddess as his wife. [note: if it's not obvious, these are the Proto-Indo-Europeans, and that god is the Dyeus archetype who precedes Zeus, Dyaus Pita, etc]</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"u